    "https://jobs.tcu.edu/jobs/search/staff-jobs": {
      "title": "Staff Jobs",
      "description": "Staff Jobs Home Faculty TCU Faculty Experience View Faculty Opportunities Staff TCU Staff Experience View Staff Opportunities Why TCU? View All Jobs APPLICANT LOGIN Kiosk mode Staff Jobs Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 8 filter options found Category Academic Support / Research (4 items) 4 Clerical / Office Staff (8 items) 8 Craft / Trades Staff (9 items) 9 Managerial / Administration (5 items) 5 Police / Campus Security (3 items) 3 Professional Staff (7 items) 7 Technology (1 items) 1 Temporary (10 items) 10 Employment Type Search employment types 2 filter options found Employment Type Full-time (25 items) 25 Temporary (12 items) 12 College/Unit Search 17 filter options found College/Unit Athletics (2 items) 2 Brite Divinity School (2 items) 2 Campus Life (2 items) 2 College of Education (2 items) 2 College of Fine Arts (5 items) 5 College of Science & Engineering (2 items) 2 Enrollment Management (2 items) 2 Facilities (7 items) 7 Harris College of Nursing & Health Sciences (1 items) 1 Information Technology (1 items) 1 Library (1 items) 1 M.J. Neeley School of Business (1 items) 1 Marketing and Communication (1 items) 1 Student Affairs (5 items) 5 University Advancement (1 items) 1 Vice Provost (1 items) 1 Vice Provost of Research (1 items) 1 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Administrative Assistant - Karyn Purvis Institute of Child Development 501274 TCU Main Campus Clerical / Office Staff Full-time College of Science & Engineering The Administrative Assistant is responsible for providing administrative support by coordinating activities, supporting programs and facilitating department objectives. Read more Administrative Program Specialist 501278 TCU Main Campus Clerical / Office Staff Full-time Student Affairs The Administrative Program Specialist provides administrative and operational support for the University Unions department by coordinating departmental processes, programs, and initiatives that support the department’s goals and objectives. Read more Campus Chaplain 501275 Brite Divinity School Professional Staff Full-time Brite Divinity School The Campus Chaplain at Brite Divinity School nurtures a spiritually vibrant, inclusive, and justice-oriented community by offering pastoral care, curating worship experiences, supporting student spiritual formation, and collaborating across institutional life. The Chaplain will serve a theologically diverse population and must be committed to ecumenical engagement, interfaith respect, and the values of equity and inclusion. The Campus Chaplain has to be able to help create a safe, integrity-based culture that launches students into the world beyond the walls of the school. This position will be a cornerstone in the community of Brite and will be an anchor to how we inspire individuals to serve God’s diverse world as leaders in churches, academia, and public life. Read more Administrative Assistant - College of Fine Arts 501270 TCU Main Campus Clerical / Office Staff Full-time College of Fine Arts The Administrative Assistant is responsible for providing administrative support by coordinating activities, supporting programs and facilitating department objectives. This position will support the Department of Fashion Merchandising. Read more Administrative Assistant - Admissions 501272 TCU Main Campus Clerical / Office Staff Full-time Enrollment Management ** This is an internal job posting intended for current TCU employees only. **\n\nThe Administrative Assistant is responsible for providing administrative support by coordinating activities, supporting programs and facilitating department objectives. Read more Administrative Support (Temp) 501113 TCU Main Campus Clerical / Office Staff Temporary Temporary Vice Provost The Administrative Support is responsible for providing administrative support to both the Academic Advising office and the Centralized Accommodated Testing Spaces by coordinating activities, supporting programs, and facilitating department objectives. Read more Director College of Fine Arts Academic Resource Center 501264 TCU Main Campus Managerial / Administration Full-time College of Fine Arts The Director of the College of Fine Arts Academic Resource Center is responsible for directing the College of Fine Arts Academic Resource Center by managing undergraduate and graduate academic advising for College of Fine Arts majors, coordinating retention strategies, and developing student development activities. Read more Budget Coordinator - School of Music 501250 TCU Main Campus Professional Staff Full-time College of Fine Arts ** This is an internal job posting intended for current TCU employees only. **\nThe Budget Coordinator is responsible for developing procedures for and processing of School of Music accounts payables, reimbursements, deposits (including online payment processing), purchasing card transactions, contract budget approvals, wire transfers, student workers payroll, temporary workers payroll, non-exempt workers overtime payroll, part-time faculty contracts, budget reconciliations and journal entry corrections, financial record archiving and establishing financial services project fund reporting.  This position will also identify opportunities for budget efficiency and savings, and communicate regularly with the Director about all unit fiscal matters. Read more Gift Processing Specialist 501263 TCU Main Campus Clerical / Office Staff Full-time University Advancement The Gift Processing Specialist is an integral part of the University Advancement team, having primary responsibility for receiving, recording, and receipting gifts to Texas Christian University. Read more Simulation Teaching Assistant 501249 TCU Main Campus Professional Staff Full-time Harris College of Nursing & Health Sciences The Simulation Teaching Associate serves in a professional staff position as a member of the Health Professions Learning Center (HPLC) team.  This role is responsible for supporting daily operations of the HPLC and assists with student skill performance and other aspects of student learning under the supervision of a faculty member. The Simulation Teaching Associate collaborates with faculty and staff to enhance learning in lab and simulation settings and provides expertise to include, but not limited to, scenario staging, appropriate supplies, and operation of healthcare simulation technology, high-fidelity manikins, procedural task trainers and other clinical equipment. Read more Executive Director Neeley Marketing & Communications 501248 TCU Main Campus Managerial / Administration Full-time M.J. Neeley School of Business The Executive Director for Marketing & Communications provides strategic leadership for the Neeley School’s marketing, communication, brand, and reputation-building activities. Working collaboratively with stakeholders within the Neeley School and across the University, the Executive Director develops and executes an integrated marketing and communication strategy that advances the School’s strategic priorities, strengthens its reputation, and engages key internal and external audiences. This role reports directly to the Dean and serves as a member of the Dean’s leadership team. This role also has a dotted line relationship to the TCU Vice Chancellor for Marketing & Communication. Read more Union Operations Mover Technician 501247 TCU Main Campus Craft / Trades Staff Full-time Facilities The Union Operations Mover Technician is responsible for performing routine conversions of staging, flooring, display builds, event space seating configurations/systems, and other various events. Responsible for the physical setup of all areas around the BLUU/KFC including flooring, chairs, tables, walls, staging, furnishings, and equipment including audio video equipment and concert staging set-ups. Read more IRB Compliance Analyst 501268 TCU Main Campus Academic Support / Research Temporary Temporary Vice Provost of Research The IRB Compliance Analyst provides administrative and regulatory support for the Human Research Protection Program (HRPP) and Institutional Review Board (IRB). The position assists with intake, pre-review, coordination, tracking, and processing of human subjects research submissions in Cayuse Human Ethics, including initial studies, modifications, continuing reviews, renewals, closures, reliance-related activities, and reportable events/incidents. The analyst supports investigators and research staff by facilitating compliance with institutional policies and applicable human subjects research regulations under the direction of the Director of Research Compliance. Complex, novel, or high-risk regulatory matters are referred to the Director of Research Compliance for review and determination. This is a temporary, hourly position approved for limited-capacity support and is capped at an average of 29 hours per week. Read more Tutor 501131 TCU Main Campus Academic Support / Research Temporary Temporary Athletics The Tutor is responsible for providing individual and small group tutoring to student-athletes in the AASO facilities, and assisting in improving academic achievement by meeting with student-athletes on a regular basis to clarify learning problems and work on study skills. Other assistance might include: reviewing class material, discussing the text, preparing for tests, brainstorming ideas for papers, or working on solutions to practice problems. Tutoring is a supplement to classroom instruction. The Tutor will report to their assigned Learning Specialist and/or the Tutor Coordinator.\n\nThis is a part-time position. Applying for this position will add you to the applicant pool, which is available to the search committee for consideration when the need arises for the 2026-2027 year. Your application will be held until May 31, 2027. Read more Dispatcher - Temporary 501103 TCU Main Campus Police / Campus Security Temporary Temporary Student Affairs The Dispatcher is responsible for coordinating the flow of incoming and outgoing information by answering calls and directing information to the appropriate channels. Read more Academic Coach 501130 TCU Main Campus Academic Support / Research Temporary Temporary Athletics The Academic Coach is responsible for reinforcing the Athletic Academic Services Office (AASO) commitment to transformative education by helping student-athletes with learning strategies, organization, study skills and alignment of their academic priorities. Academic Coaches work with identified student-athletes based on recent matriculation, developing academic achievement and/or learning differences. Academic Coaches seek to model appropriate behavior for learning, provide customized instruction and guide student-athletes through the learning process. The Academic Coach will report to their assigned Learning Specialist and/or the Tutor Coordinator.\n\nThis is a part-time position. Applying for this position will add you to the applicant pool, which is available to the search committee for consideration when the need arises for the 2026-2027 year. Your application will be held until May 31, 2027. Read more Grounds Assistant - Temporary 500917 TCU Main Campus Craft / Trades Staff Temporary Temporary Facilities Temporary (Summer Only): \n\nThe Grounds Assistant is responsible for aiding in all facets of landscaping and grounds as part of the grounds team. Read more Lifeguard - Temporary 500888 TCU Main Campus Professional Staff Temporary Temporary Campus Life The Lifeguard ensures the safety of patrons of the aquatic facility by preventing and responding to emergencies. Read more Security Guard - Temporary 500964 TCU Main Campus Police / Campus Security Temporary Temporary Student Affairs The Security Guard is responsible for maintaining safe and secure environment by observing activities, patrolling areas, identifying traffic violations. Read more Residential Housekeeping - Area Supervisor 501088 TCU Main Campus Craft / Trades Staff Full-time Student Affairs The Area Supervisor is responsible for leading daily residential housekeeping operations while serving as a working supervisor. This role provides direct supervision, coaching, and accountability for assigned staff while actively supporting cleaning operations to ensure service continuity. The Supervisor is expected to perform housekeeping duties as needed to maintain service levels, respond to staffing gaps, and support team productivity. This position participates in an on-call rotation and is available for call-back responsibilities to support after-hours and emergency operational needs. Read more IT Purchasing Specialist 501245 TCU Main Campus Technology Full-time Information Technology The IT Purchasing Specialist is responsible for procuring Technology equipment, software, software as a service, and IT professional services by coordinating requests, researching and completing orders. Read more Manager of University Events and Community Projects 501237 TCU Main Campus Managerial / Administration Full-time Marketing and Communication The Manager of University Events and Community Projects is responsible for managing internal and external groups utilizing campus facilities; marketing facilities; identifying service needs; supporting daily event operations. Read more Director of Undergraduate Admissions 501239 TCU Main Campus Managerial / Administration Full-time Enrollment Management The Director of Undergraduate Admission is responsible for supporting the undergraduate admission processes by assisting in planning and executing policy and programming, recommending admission actions, and supervising Associate Directors of Admission. The Director of Undergraduate Admission will be a strategic partner in the development of a comprehensive recruitment plan informed by data best practices. Purview will contain domestic first-year and transfer admission and international admission. Read more Program Office Coordinator (FROG Care Clinics) 501198 TCU Main Campus Clerical / Office Staff Full-time College of Education The FROG Care Clinics Program Office Coordinator provides administrative and operational support to ensure efficient, compliant, and organized functioning of the clinic’s day-to-day operations. This role supports front-end systems, referral coordination, administrative relationships between partners, training infrastructure, and regulatory compliance, including HIPAA. Read more Dean - Science & Engineering 501187 TCU Main Campus Managerial / Administration Full-time College of Science & Engineering The Dean for the College of Science and Engineering is responsible for providing thoughtful and innovative leadership in the areas of strategic and visionary long-range planning, budgetary management, personnel selection and evaluation, programmatic and curriculum review and development, assessment, development of financial resources including external fundraising and research grants, facilitates the teacher-scholar model and desired student outcomes and represents the college effectively within the University and the larger community, at the local and national level. Read more Librarian I - Web Services 501203 TCU Main Campus Professional Staff Full-time Library The Librarian I (Web Services) is responsible for designing and maintaining library web sites and web-based applications, with a focus on content and user interface accessibility and usability. They assist other library staff with creating accessible online content, including instruction and marketing materials. They work with the Director of Automated Systems, Systems Manager, and other Systems staff to evaluate and enhance the library online catalog and other discovery interfaces. Read more Grounds Equipment Operator 500680 TCU Main Campus Craft / Trades Staff Full-time Facilities ** This is an internal job posting intended for current TCU employees only. **\nThe Grounds Equipment Operator is responsible for maintaining the landscaping at TCU. Read more High School College Advisor 500921 TCU Main Campus Academic Support / Research Full-time College of Education The High School College Advisor assists Texas high school students in underserved communities in realizing their dream of attending college by advising students with college admissions, financial aid, and scholarship applications; coordinating information with high school staff at the student’s school. Read more Admission Counselor 501147 Brite Divinity School Professional Staff Full-time Brite Divinity School The Admission Counselor is an outcome-driven position primarily responsible for recruitment and outreach efforts that increase inquiries, applications, and enrollment at Brite Divinity School. This position cultivates relationships with prospective students, campus ministries, faith communities, community organizations, alumni, and other theological education partners.\n\nThe Counselor serves as a visible representative of Brite at recruitment events, conferences, graduate fairs, churches, and online platforms, while also providing admissions counseling and support throughout the enrollment pipeline. The position requires strong relational skills, strategic communication, and the ability to recruit across diverse communities and contexts. Read more Service Assistant - Facilities 500977 TCU Main Campus Craft / Trades Staff Full-time Facilities The Service Assistant is responsible for maintaining campus buildings by providing cleaning services. Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 37 in total ‹ 1 2 › Human Resources 2701 W. Berry Street Fort Worth, Texas 76109 Phone: 817-257-7790 TCU Box 298200 Fort Worth, Texas 76129 Quick Links Home Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Other Opportunities Why TCU? Applicant Login Work at TCU Accessibility Notice of Nondiscrimination Title IX Legal Disclosures Privacy Accreditation All content © 2023 Texas Christian University . All rights reserved. Top Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept"
    },
