lty Full-time M.J. Neeley School of Business This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. Texas Christian University invites applications for the non-tenure track position of Instructor of Analytics/Statistics in the Department of Information Systems and Supply Chain Management (INSC) in the Neeley School of Business beginning August 2027. We are looking for a colleague with a rich background in the following areas: Analytics, Artificial Intelligence /Machine Learning, Information Systems, Statistics. Read more Administrative Support (Temp) 501113 TCU Main Campus Clerical / Office Staff Temporary Temporary Vice Provost The Administrative Support is responsible for providing administrative support to both the Academic Advising office and the Centralized Accommodated Testing Spaces by coordinating activities, supporting programs, and facilitating department objectives. Read more Director College of Fine Arts Academic Resource Center 501264 TCU Main Campus Managerial / Administration Full-time College of Fine Arts The Director of the College of Fine Arts Academic Resource Center is responsible for directing the College of Fine Arts Academic Resource Center by managing undergraduate and graduate academic advising for College of Fine Arts majors, coordinating retention strategies, and developing student development activities. Read more Budget Coordinator - School of Music 501250 TCU Main Campus Professional Staff Full-time College of Fine Arts ** This is an internal job posting intended for current TCU employees only. **\nThe Budget Coordinator is responsible for developing procedures for and processing of School of Music accounts payables, reimbursements, deposits (including online payment processing), purchasing card transactions, contract budget approvals, wire transfers, student workers payroll, temporary workers payroll, non-exempt workers overtime payroll, part-time faculty contracts, budget reconciliations and journal entry corrections, financial record archiving and establishing financial services project fund reporting.  This position will also identify opportunities for budget efficiency and savings, and communicate regularly with the Director about all unit fiscal matters. Read more Gift Processing Specialist 501263 TCU Main Campus Clerical / Office Staff Full-time University Advancement The Gift Processing Specialist is an integral part of the University Advancement team, having primary responsibility for receiving, recording, and receipting gifts to Texas Christian University. Read more Simulation Teaching Assistant 501249 TCU Main Campus Professional Staff Full-time Harris College of Nursing & Health Sciences The Simulation Teaching Associate serves in a professional staff position as a member of the Health Professions Learning Center (HPLC) team.  This role is responsible for supporting daily operations of the HPLC and assists with student skill performance and other aspects of student learning under the supervision of a faculty member. The Simulation Teaching Associate collaborates with faculty and staff to enhance learning in lab and simulation settings and provides expertise to include, but not limited to, scenario staging, appropriate supplies, and operation of healthcare simulation technology, high-fidelity manikins, procedural task trainers and other clinical equipment. Read more Executive Director Neeley Marketing & Communications 501248 TCU Main Campus Managerial / Administration Full-time M.J. Neeley School of Business The Executive Director for Marketing & Communications provides strategic leadership for the Neeley School’s marketing, communication, brand, and reputation-building activities. Working collaboratively with stakeholders within the Neeley School and across the University, the Executive Director develops and executes an integrated marketing and communication strategy that advances the School’s strategic priorities, strengthens its reputation, and engages key internal and external audiences. This role reports directly to the Dean and serves as a member of the Dean’s leadership team. This role also has a dotted line relationship to the TCU Vice Chancellor for Marketing & Communication. Read more Union Operations Mover Technician 501247 TCU Main Campus Craft / Trades Staff Full-time Facilities The Union Operations Mover Technician is responsible for performing routine conversions of staging, flooring, display builds, event space seating configurations/systems, and other various events. Responsible for the physical setup of all areas around the BLUU/KFC including flooring, chairs, tables, walls, staging, furnishings, and equipment including audio video equipment and concert staging set-ups. Read more IRB Compliance Analyst 501268 TCU Main Campus Academic Support / Research Temporary Temporary Vice Provost of Research The IRB Compliance Analyst provides administrative and regulatory support for the Human Research Protection Program (HRPP) and Institutional Review Board (IRB). The position assists with intake, pre-review, coordination, tracking, and processing of human subjects research submissions in Cayuse Human Ethics, including initial studies, modifications, continuing reviews, renewals, closures, reliance-related activities, and reportable events/incidents. The analyst supports investigators and research staff by facilitating compliance with institutional policies and applicable human subjects research regulations under the direction of the Director of Research Compliance. Complex, novel, or high-risk regulatory matters are referred to the Director of Research Compliance for review and determination. This is a temporary, hourly position approved for limited-capacity support and is capped at an average of 29 hours per week. Read more Tutor 501131 TCU Main Campus Academic Support / Research Temporary Temporary Athletics The Tutor is responsible for providing individual and small group tutoring to student-athletes in the AASO facilities, and assisting in improving academic achievement by meeting with student-athletes on a regular basis to clarify learning problems and work on study skills. Other assistance might include: reviewing class material, discussing the text, preparing for tests, brainstorming ideas for papers, or working on solutions to practice problems. Tutoring is a supplement to classroom instruction. The Tutor will report to their assigned Learning Specialist and/or the Tutor Coordinator.\n\nThis is a part-time position. Applying for this position will add you to the applicant pool, which is available to the search committee for consideration when the need arises for the 2026-2027 year. Your application will be held until May 31, 2027. Read more Dispatcher - Temporary 501103 TCU Main Campus Police / Campus Security Temporary Temporary Student Affairs The Dispatcher is responsible for coordinating the flow of incoming and outgoing information by answering calls and directing information to the appropriate channels. Read more Academic Coach 501130 TCU Main Campus Academic Support / Research Temporary Temporary Athletics The Academic Coach is responsible for reinforcing the Athletic Academic Services Office (AASO) commitment to transformative education by helping student-athletes with learning strategies, organization, study skills and alignment of their academic priorities. Academic Coaches work with identified student-athletes based on recent matriculation, developing academic achievement and/or learning differences. Academic Coaches seek to model appropriate behavior for learning, provide customized instruction and guide student-athletes through the learning process. The Academic Coach will report to their assigned Learning Specialist and/or the Tutor Coordinator.\n\nThis is a part-time position. Applying for this position will add you to the applicant pool, which is available to the search committee for consideration when the need arises for the 2026-2027 year. Your application will be held until May 31, 2027. Read more Grounds Assistant - Temporary 500917 TCU Main Campus Craft / Trades Staff Temporary Temporary Facilities Temporary (Summer Only): \n\nThe Grounds Assistant is responsible for aiding in all facets of landscaping and grounds as part of the grounds team. Read more Lifeguard - Temporary 500888 TCU Main Campus Professional Staff Temporary Temporary Campus Life The Lifeguard ensures the safety of patrons of the aquatic facility by preventing and responding to emergencies. Read more Security Guard - Temporary 500964 TCU Main Campus Police / Campus Security Temporary Temporary Student Affairs The Security Guard is responsible for maintaining safe and secure environment by observing activities, patrolling areas, identifying traffic violations. Read more Residential Housekeeping - Area Supervisor 501088 TCU Main Campus Craft / Trades Staff Full-time Student Affairs The Area Supervisor is responsible for leading daily residential housekeeping operations while serving as a working supervisor. This role provides direct supervision, coaching, and accountability for assigned staff while actively supporting cleaning operations to ensure service continuity. The Supervisor is expected to perform housekeeping duties as needed to maintain service levels, respond to staffing gaps, and support team productivity. This position participates in an on-call rotation and is available for call-back responsibilities to support after-hours and emergency operational needs. Read more IT Purchasing Specialist 501245 TCU Main Campus Technology Full-time Information Technology The IT Purchasing Specialist is responsible for procuring Technology equipment, software, software as a service, and IT professional services by coordinating requests, researching and completing orders. Read more Assistant or Associate Professor of Psychology 501242 TCU Main Campus Faculty Full-time College of Science & Engineering HEALTH PSYCHOLOGY FACULTY POSITION AVAILABLE\n\nThis full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. The TCU Department of Psychology is hiring a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor beginning August 2027. This position is part of a broader strategic initiative to build a nationally recognized research program focused on health and well-being. Primary consideration will be given to candidates who have completed a Ph.D. in any area of Psychology. We are particularly interested in health psychology research focused on addiction science, digital technologies and artificial intelligence (AI), intervention/implementation science, aging, behavioral science/medicine, or biomedical approaches, but we welcome applications from all areas of psychology. Application Deadline: 10/1/2026 Read more Director of the Institute of Ranch Management and Associate Professor of Professional Practice in Ranch Management 501241 TCU Main Campus Faculty Full-time College of Science & Engineering The TCU Ranch Management Program invites applications for the William Watt Matthews Director of the Institute of Ranch Management and Associate Professor of Professional Practice in Ranch Management, a leadership position at one of the nation's premier ranch management programs. The Director will shape industry partnerships, advance applied agricultural education, and prepare the next generation of ranch and agricultural business leaders. The Ranch Management Institute's primary function is to establish industry partnerships and conduct educational outreach for the TCU Ranch Management program. Read more Manager of University Events and Community Projects 501237 TCU Main Campus Managerial / Administration Full-time Marketing and Communication The Manager of University Events and Community Projects is responsible for managing internal and external groups utilizing campus facilities; marketing facilities; identifying service needs; supporting daily event operations. Read more Director of Undergraduate Admissions 501239 TCU Main Campus Managerial / Administration Full-time Enrollment Management The Director of Undergraduate Admission is responsible for supporting the undergraduate admission processes by assisting in planning and executing policy and programming, recommending admission actions, and supervising Associate Directors of Admission. The Director of Undergraduate Admission will be a strategic partner in the development of a comprehensive recruitment plan informed by data best practices. Purview will contain domestic first-year and transfer admission and international admission. Read more Assistant/Associate Professor or Assistant/Associate Professor of Professional Practice - Occupational Therapy 500889 TCU Main Campus Faculty Full-time Harris College of Nursing & Health Sciences The Harris College of Nursing & Health Sciences invites applications for one 12-month faculty position as a Tenure-Track Assistant/Associate Professor or Assistant/Associate Professor of Professional Practice (non-tenure) for the developing entry-level Doctor of Occupational Therapy (OTD) Program at Texas Christian University (TCU). Read more Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Chemistry 501167 TCU Main Campus Faculty Full-time College of Science & Engineering This full-time faculty position is on-campus and in-person. \n\nThe Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry is conducting an open search for a tenure-track or tenured position in chemistry or aligned fields adopting a molecular perspective. While candidates from any subdiscipline are encouraged to apply, emphasis will be placed on individuals with backgrounds in inorganic or bioinorganic chemistry. Read more Program Office Coordinator (FROG Care Clinics) 501198 TCU Main Campus Clerical / Office Staff Full-time College of Education The FROG Care Clinics Program Office Coordinator provides administrative and operational support to ensure efficient, compliant, and organized functioning of the clinic’s day-to-day operations. This role supports front-end systems, referral coordination, administrative relationships between partners, training infrastructure, and regulatory compliance, including HIPAA. Read more Dean - Science & Engineering 501187 TCU Main Campus Managerial / Administration Full-time College of Science & Engineering The Dean for the College of Science and Engineering is responsible for providing thoughtful and innovative leadership in the areas of strategic and visionary long-range planning, budgetary management, personnel selection and evaluation, programmatic and curriculum review and development, assessment, development of financial resources including external fundraising and research grants, facilitates the teacher-scholar model and desired student outcomes and represents the college effectively within the University and the larger community, at the local and national level. Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 120 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 › Human Resources 2701 W. Berry Street Fort Worth, Texas 76109 Phone: 817-257-7790 TCU Box 298200 Fort Worth, Texas 76129 Quick Links Home Faculty Jobs Staff Jobs Other Opportunities Why TCU? Applicant Login Work at TCU Accessibility Notice of Nondiscrimination Title IX Legal Disclosures Privacy Accreditation All content © 2023 Texas Christian University . All rights reserved. Top Candidate Details TCU uses \"cookies\" (i.e., a small text file that is sent to your browser from the Site) to improve your return access and visits to the Site. TCU may use cookies to customize content, to analyze Site activity and user behavior, including, without limitation, through Google Analytics Demographics and Interest Reporting, and for advertising and promotional purposes (further discussed in \"Interest-based Advertising\" below). TCU reserves the right to use cookies in the future in conjunction with new or extended functionalities. Privacy Policy I do not accept I accept"
    },
